From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Suno <engineering@projectSuno.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] SunoUI: Suno account › Sync (Suno Connect Sync)

Suno Connect Sync (ADR-054) in Settings, as design-center 38858a5
(mockups/connect-sync) draws it, read from Suno-connect-syncd
(org.projectSuno.ConnectSync1) by a new adapter, "sync", as CFSYNC:
GetState, ListApps and ListDevices, again on StateChanged and AppsChanged
(an unchanged reading redraws nothing). Its keys: "syncOn" (SetEnabled), "syncCat" (SetCategory),
"syncApp" (SetAppEnabled).

Page "sync" under the Suno account ("‹ Suno Connect"): the hero with the
state tile, state and line, the main switch and the storage bar ("1.8 GB of
5 GB", by kind beside it except on a phone), the lock line, What syncs (one
switch per category), App data (the four biggest apps, "size · state", the
"Uses Suno Connect" tag and Delete synced data for Sync API apps, "All N
apps" to page "sync-apps"), Devices (class icon, "Class · synced …",
Remove… with its confirm) and Recovery key (Show…, RevealRecoveryKey).
The account page gets a Suno Connect group with a row to it.

Turning Sync on: BeginSetup, then a sheet: the 24 words numbered in a well
(4 columns, 3 on a phone), Save as a file… and Print…, no Copy; Continue
waits for the tick; Cancel, Esc and the scrim call CancelSetup and leave
Sync off; three words typed back gate Turn on Sync (FinishSetup,
SetEnabled). A device joining an account that has Sync asks RequestJoin and
waits with the code in two wells and the devices that can approve, or takes
the recovery key ("18 of 24 words", JoinWithRecoveryKey; a wrong key's
message under the field). Turning Sync off asks first. The Shell opens the
page with ('users', ['sync']) and the join sheet with ('users', ['sync',
'join']). Phone: a bottom drawer with stacked 44 px actions; TV: 1.5 times,
focus on Cancel.

Fixtures carry CFSYNC and may name Suno-v4-* artwork beside them;
SUNO_SETTINGS_SYNC_SHEET shows one sheet alone (conform). Test:
Suno-settings-connect-sync.
